DESCRIPTION:This Full Moon lands in your first house of identity\, opposit
 e the Sun in your house of partnership. It's a moment where who you are (M
 oon\, house 1) meets who you are becoming through others (Sun\, house 7). 
 Neptune sits right on this Moon\, softening boundaries and heightening int
 uition\, maybe blurring where you end and someone else begins. Mars\, the 
 ruler of this Aries Moon\, lives naturally in your house of philosophy and
  travel\, but is currently energizing your house of work and routines\, so
  the insight you gain here wants to be grounded in daily action\, not just
  dreamed about. This closes the cycle from the New Moon of April 2026\, in
  the same sign: revisit what you intended then about yourself. What has ac
 tually shifted in how you show up\, versus how you appear in relationship?
  → Which intention from last April deserves an honest\, grounded update 
 now?\n\n— Technical detail: Full Moon · 3°37' Aries · house 1 · exac
 t 26/09 18:49
